This algorithm is an algorithm which is used when we have to deal with subsets. when the array is large and we have to generate all the subsets, 
then the time complexity will be very high. 

lets suppose we have an array of length 4. so the number of subsets will be 2^4 which is 16. 
this is ok
but if the array is of length 40 then the number of subsets will be 2^40 which is approximately 1 trillion. 

and it is almost impossible to handle 1 million subsets.

here is where the meet in the middle algorithm comes into picture. 
in this algorithm we divide the array into 2 halves. lets suppose the length of array is 40. 
so the length of the first half is 20 and the second half is also 20. 

